@startuml control-studio
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam linetype ortho

title truST Control Studio: Reused Runtime And Simulation Flow

package "VS Code webview" {
  component "Control Studio workflow\nMonitor / Test / Identify /\nTune / Validate" as workflow
  component "Shared ECharts adapter\nformatted bounded display data" as charts
}

package "VS Code extension host" {
  component "Control Studio panel\nstrict loop-scoped messages" as panel
  component "Loop monitor" as monitor
  component "Experiment client" as experiment
  component "Identify / tune / validate\npure functions" as analysis
  component "Runtime lifecycle" as lifecycle
  component "Existing runtime\ncontrol client" as client
  database "VS Code workspace state\nactive experiment identity +\nsaved workflow result" as workspace_state
}

package "Existing runtime" {
  component "Debug/runtime control server" as control
  component "One process-image\nsnapshot stream" as process_image
  component "Existing SimulationController" as simulation
  component "Control.PID instance" as pid
}

workflow --> panel : versioned commands
panel --> workflow : loop-scoped results
workflow --> charts
panel --> monitor
panel --> experiment
panel --> analysis
panel --> workspace_state : minimal reload recovery
monitor --> lifecycle
experiment --> lifecycle
lifecycle --> client : active endpoint + token
client --> control : existing request transport
control --> process_image
process_image --> monitor : SP / PV / MV snapshot
process_image --> pid
simulation --> process_image : pre/post scan I/O

note right of workspace_state
No artifact database.
Raw recordings and the accepted result
remain project-scoped and reproducible.
end note

note bottom of experiment
The runtime owns start, abort, timeout and restore.
Reload recovery polls the same experiment identity;
it never starts a second excitation.
end note

note bottom of control
Physical excitation and controller apply require
their existing explicit approval boundaries.
Simulation evidence is labelled separately.
end note

@enduml
